Windows User Account & Permissions Management
Project Overview
This project demonstrates practical Windows 11 administration skills, including local user account creation, password management, folder permissions and user access testing.

Tools Used
Windows 11
Command Prompt (Administrator)
File Explorer
Windows Security Properties
Practical Tasks
1. Create a Local User Account
Command:
net user LvUser * /add

Created a local Windows account named LvUser with a password.

2. Verify User Account
Command:
net user LvUser

Verified the account information and confirmed that the account was active.

3. Create a Folder
Created a folder named LvUserFiles for the permissions exercise.

4. Configure Folder Permissions
Added LvUser to the folder’s Security permissions.

Granted:

Read
Write
Read & Execute
List Folder Contents
Full Control and Modify were not granted.

5. Test User Access
Signed in using the LvUser account and tested access to the designated folder.

6. Create and Open a Test Document
Created LabUser_Test.txt and successfully opened the document.

Skills Practised
Windows user administration
Command-line operations
NTFS permissions
Access control
File management
User access testing
Project Outcome
Successfully created and verified a local Windows user account, configured folder permissions and tested document access.

